/archive/

# Bridge Config
**/bridge.config.json

# Chatterbox
**/chatterbox/config.yaml
**/chatterbox/logs
**/chatterbox/outputs

# Caddy
**/Caddyfile

# Caddy TLS certs (hosting/caddy/certs/) — nothing in there is tracked.
# Cloudflare origin pair (user-supplied):
**/cloudflare-key.pem
**/cloudflare.pem
# Your own public-domain wildcard pair (Caddyfile.frontdoor-public.example):
**/public-key.pem
**/public.pem
# Stable *.internal cert + CA, minted by caddy/exist.initial.sh (keys are secret;
# certs are host-local generated artifacts — none are committed):
**/internal-ca-key.pem
**/internal-ca.pem
**/internal-key.pem
**/internal.pem
**/internal.csr
**/internal-ca.srl

# Code-server
**/opencode.json
workspace

# Dashy
# dashy-conf.yml is regenerated on every run, unless the user claims it by
# flipping EXIST_KEEP to true in its header — either way it is theirs, not ours.
**/dashy-conf.yml

# Decree
**/decree/webhook/config.yml
# throwaway binary built by webhook/difftest.sh
**/decree/webhook/.difftest-webhook
# `go build` in webhook/ drops the compiled binary here (named for the module).
# The image builds it from source in a multi-stage Dockerfile and .dockerignore
# denies it from the build context, so a committed copy is pure dead weight.
**/decree/webhook/decree-webhook
automations/lib/file-processors/*
automations/runs/*
automations/secrets/*
# Per-decree-daemon runtime state. There are two daemon project dirs, both under
# services/decree/: decree/ (the main daemon) and decree-backup/ (backups), so
# each pattern below is repeated for decree-backup/.
**/decree/config.yml
**/decree-backup/config.yml
**/decree-backup/config.hash
**/decree-backup/cron/*
**/decree-backup/migrations/*
**/decree-backup/data/*
**/decree-backup/inbox/*
**/decree-backup/outbox/
**/decree-backup/processed.md
**/decree-backup/precheck.log
**/decree-backup/shared_routines/*
**/decree-backup/lib/*
**/decree-backup/runs/*
**/decree/config.hash
**/decree/cron/*
# Activated migrations are the user's copies of migrations.example/ — same
# contract as cron/: the example is tracked, the activated copy is local.
**/decree/migrations/*
**/decree/data/*
**/decree/emails/
**/decree/inbox/*
**/decree/outbox/
**/decree/processed.md
# Per-daemon runtime output. precheck.log records which routines passed their
# DECREE_PRE_CHECK at startup, so it is regenerated on every boot.
**/decree/precheck.log
# The host-side outbox some routines write to when they run outside a container.
# Its dead/ holds FULL message bodies — user content and model output — and it
# sits outside the **/decree/ patterns above, so it needs naming.
automations/outbox/
# Nested bind-mount points — dirs tracked (.gitkeep force-added), content ignored.
# These must exist before first `docker compose up` so Docker doesn't auto-create them as root.
**/decree/shared_routines/*
**/decree/lib/*
**/decree/runs/*

